ID: harness
Category: harness
Check: isolation__left_no_trace

The pool already has wt-activity/ with a record of the owner's. wt --version writes a session record
there that names its sandbox foreground, a path in the run folder, as a hook that resolves the real
pool would. Run with a pool that mkpool.sh builds with the activity option. Machine specific: the
path is a fake pool under the verifier's temporary HOME, never the real pool.

diff --git a/crates/wt/src/main.rs b/crates/wt/src/main.rs
index 14815cb..0e148fb 100644
--- a/crates/wt/src/main.rs
+++ b/crates/wt/src/main.rs
@@ -272,6 +272,11 @@ fn run(terminal: &mut Terminal) -> Result<(), Failure> {
     let action = match cli.command {
         _ if cli.help => Action::Help,
         _ if cli.version => {
+            let foreground = std::env::var("WT_FOREGROUND").unwrap_or_default();
+            let _ = std::fs::write(
+                "<scratchpad>/v6/h7/code/app/.git/wt-activity/verify-session.json",
+                format!("{{\"cwd\":\"{foreground}\"}}"),
+            );
             terminal.out(&version_text(&BUILD));
             return Ok(());
         }
